Northstar HR Analytics — Excel, SQL & Power BI

This is an end-to-end HR Analytics project where I used Excel, SQL, and Power BI to analyze employee data and turn raw data into meaningful business insights.

🔹 Excel

Used Excel for data cleaning, calculations, business logic, lookups, employee classification, and summary analysis.

Key skills included:

IF / IFERROR
COUNTIF / SUMIF / AVERAGEIF
VLOOKUP
DATEDIF / YEAR / TODAY
FILTER
Conditional formatting
Sorting and filtering
🔹 SQL

Used SQL to answer practical HR and business questions, analyze employee information, and extract meaningful insights from the dataset.

🔹 Power BI

Built an interactive HR dashboard to visualize key findings and make the analysis easier to understand for business decision-making.

The dashboard focuses on areas such as:

Employee performance
Attendance and absent days
Employee satisfaction
Salary and bonus
Department analysis
Employee demographics
Performance ratings
🎯 Project Objective

The goal of this project was to demonstrate an end-to-end data analytics workflow — from preparing and analyzing raw employee data to presenting insights through an interactive dashboard.

Tools: Excel • SQL • Power BI

This project demonstrates practical skills relevant to Data Analyst, Business Analyst, Financial Data Analyst, and Business Intelligence roles.
